touchdown  hayden hurst meanwhile he's going to  wind up hitting him first here  for a touchdown  dear hayden get ready this is going to  be a wild 10 years  no one could have imagined the twists  turns ups and downs the crash  and the resurrection like your beloved  phoenix  life will be radiant and shining then  suddenly you'll burst into flames  and nearly die only to be reborn from  the ashes to become a first-round nfl  pick  [Applause]  shortly after your 14th birthday the  accolades will come  throwing in the upper 80s as a pitcher  the local sports anchor will do a tv  segment on you  but during that throwing session you'll  feel a pop and your velocity will begin  to lag  a month later dr andrews the top  orthopedic surgeon in the country  performs tommy john's surgery on you 12  months after the surgery you're on the  mound again  and then the roller coaster takes off  kennedy fires a pass complete  in high school you'll play both football  and baseball and by your senior year  you'll be one of the top pitchers in the  country you're projected to be a late  first or early second round pick in the  mlb draft  but when the time comes you'll wait two  days to hear your name called  it will damage your ego  the pittsburgh pirates will grab you in  the 17th round  and off you'll go as a 19 year old for  your first  year in minor league baseball hard  throwing  right-hander hayden hurst but tighten up  life will spiral  downward from here you'll develop the  yips  ruining your ability to throw with  accuracy  you'll tumble into depression and spend  thousands of dollars on therapy  but it will all fail you  you'll turn to alcohol and drugs to kill  the pain  you'll be in a precipitous free fall and  that will bring on more drugs and  nightly drinking until you black out  finally in 2015 at the age of 21  you'll leave during spring training and  retire from baseball  the baseball dream will be dead  [Music]  but there will be another road you'll  walk onto the university of south  carolina football team in the summer of  2015.  you'll have some success but the demons  of depression will still have a hold on  you  and the drugs and drinking will only  escalate after a drunken night on the  town  you'll see no escape from the darkness  and in a chaotic moment  you'll make the calamitous decision to  take your own life  while sitting in your truck one night  you'll take out a knife and cut your  wrist  but god will watch over you  and despite being almost blacked out  drunk you'll miraculously call a friend  who happens to be in nursing school  she rushes over to stop the bleeding and  calls 9-1-1  the phoenix has exploded into flames and  is now in ashes  you'll be taken to a local hospital and  stabilized then moved to a psychiatric  ward and placed on a 72-hour suicide  hold  you'll feel alone embarrassed and like  you've let everyone down  you'll make a decision right there that  you will never be in this position again  you'll tell yourself the rebirth starts  now  you decide there will be no more  drinking and no more drugs  five years later you'll have kept your  promise and be completely clean  [Music]  south carolina football will have you in  therapy for several months and you'll  make a commitment to be the best  football player that you can be  and you'll blossom into one of the top  players in the country and on april 26  2018 the crowning moment of your  comeback you'll be selected by the  baltimore ravens in the nfl draft  along the way you'll learn to lean on  friends family doctors and therapists  you'll realize that despite what you may  think you are not alone in this fight  and you'll channel your hurt sadness and  anxiety into opportunities for others  going through the same struggles  you'll start a charity and raise  hundreds of thousands of dollars for  programs that address mental health  issues  and suicide prevention in teens and  adolescents  it's going to be an unimaginable 10  years  there will be colossal highs and then a  protracted seemingly  endless journey through a personal hell  followed by an unthinkable event  it's a long tough mental fight  be ready because everyone knows  in the end the phoenix rises gloriously  from the ashes  thank you hayden hurst you saved a lot  of lives today someone is listening to  that  right now and is saying he's telling my  story  i so admire his his courage his bravery  and his candor to share that  but the most important message that i  think he says is to let people know you  are not alone  and it really does get better even when  it doesn't seem like there's no way out  and that's such an interesting thing  that's such an important point  and i've heard so many people who've  been through this say the same thing  and and want to share with other people  that you're not alone because that's the  way you feel in that moment  the capacity for transformation that we  have as human beings  is always astonishing yes yeah  men be vulnerable yes yeah yeah be  vulnerable make time for vulnerability  and reflection it's okay  it's okay we thank you kyra cleveland  who's a knockout producer here great job  adam a t  you too and lee hooper who shot it  nicely done  it takes a lot to put a piece together  like that very very very nice  if you or someone you know is  experiencing a mental health crisis  you can call the national suicide  prevention line it's 1-800-273-8255  or maybe it's easier to text hello to  741  741  you

